Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: bfd/coff64-rs6000.c
Line: 628
Function: _bfd_xcoff64_put_ldsymbol_name
Bug type: integer-overflow-to-heap-buffer-overflow
CWE: CWE-190
Explanation: The size check uses ldinfo->string_size + len + 3 to decide whether to grow ldinfo->strings, but the addition can overflow bfd_size_type. If it wraps, the reallocation may be skipped or allocated too small, and the subsequent strcpy into ldinfo->strings + ldinfo->string_size + 2 will write len+1 bytes past the end of the buffer. newalc *= 2 in the growth loop can also overflow. An attacker supplying an excessively long name can trigger this.

